  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">National Democratic Institute- 2026 Election Support</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to strengthen democratic governance in Zambia ahead of the 2026 elections. It will promote transparency, accountability, and citizen participation by supporting independent, non-partisan observation of the electoral process and advocating for key political and electoral reforms. Building on NDI&#x2019;s global expertise and CCMG&#x2019;s national credibility, the project will train and deploy observers, monitor pre-election conditions, and provide timely, evidence-based reports to the public, media, and decision-makers. It will also support civil society to respond quickly to legislative and policy changes, ensuring reforms protect civic space and reflect citizen priorities. Special focus will be placed on inclusion, ensuring women, youth, and people with disabilities are represented and their concerns addressed. By fostering collaboration among citizens, civil society, government, and the Electoral Commission of Zambia, the project seeks to safeguard democratic processes, reduce political violence, and build long-term capacity for transparent, credible elections.</narrative>
  </description>
